p.src:
To see the geometry, first discretize one coordinate with spacing $\epsilon$. A first derivative is a neighboring difference, while a second derivative is a difference of neighboring differences: $\frac{d^2X}{ds^2}\bigg|_{2}
  \longrightarrow
  \frac{X(3)-2X(2)+X(1)}{\epsilon^2}.$

